   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the education law, in relation to requiring immediate notification by law enforcement of an employee's arrest involving allegations of a sex offense",
    "basePrintNo": "S6597",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6597-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 43,
       "fullName": "Kathleen A. Marchione",
       "imgName": "435_kathleen_a._marchione.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 435,
       "sessionMemberId": 940,
       "sessionYear": 2017,
       "shortName": "MARCHIONE"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §3021-a, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6597\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the education law, in relation to\nrequiring immediate notification by law enforcement of an employee's\narrest involving allegations of a sex offense\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nRequires immediate notification by law enforcement of an employee's\narrest involving allegations of a sex offense\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Amend the education law to provide for notification to\nschool districts when an employee has been arrested for a sex offense.\n\nSection 2: Effective date\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nIt was recently reported that a custodian in a New York public school\ndistrict was convicted of raping a minor but had continued to work in\nthe school facility, in contact with students, through the course of\nthe legal process. The school district was not notified of the arrest\nor the subsequent trial because local law enforcement was not required\nto alert the school district of the arrest. The school district was\nreported to only have learned of the arrest and conviction when an\nanonymous tip was received.\n\nGiven the close proximity of school district employees to students,\nincluding custodial, contracted workers, and others, it is imperative\nthat school districts receive prompt notice of arrests involving sex\noffenses. As such, this legislation modifies the education law to\nrequire that law enforcement agencies immediately notify the\nsuperintendent of schools of an arrest and all other relevant public\ninformation pending indictment or the filing of an accusatory\ninstrument.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
